  "body_html": "<h1>Monotonic Coalitional Game</h1>\n<p>A coalitional game is <strong>monotonic</strong> if enlarging a coalition cannot reduce\nits worth. For coalitions $S \\subseteq T \\subseteq N$,\n$$\n  v(S) \\le v(T).\n$$</p>\n<p>This property is weaker than superadditivity in many standard settings but\ncaptures the same basic direction: adding players should not make a\ncoalition worse off.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MSZ Ch.16, Def 16.10] Maschler, Solan, Zamir, <em>Game Theory</em>,\n  <code>references/GameTheory.pdf</code>.</li>\n</ul>",
